{
 "_doc": "Waystation 9 (DESIGN §1, ADR-0039; TD-369): the Remand Program's trader post built into the Cordon wall where the river leaves the valley, main-map region D7 (World places it and the wall). A SAFE place, tier 1: no Hollowed, no traps, no triggers; the guards' safe zone is the trader def's (data/traders/waystation_9.json, safe_radius 40). The plan's +Z (front, rows 19-27) is the VALLEY side; rows 0-8 lie OUTSIDE the Cordon. WALL LINE: plan z = 9.0 (the edge between rows 8 and 9), from x 0 to x 36. The post's two-storey block (x 12-24, z 5-19) straddles it, and four cordon_wall_panel props (pitch 6.0) carry it from the footprint's west edge (x 0) and east edge (x 36) to the block: the region's wall continues from those two points, (0, 9) and (36, 9) in plan metres, i.e. panel centres at x -3, -9, ... and 39, 45, ... on z = 9 (rot 0 in the plan frame). Nothing on the block opens outward (no doors or windows on its north face or on the side walls north of the line), so the post is no way out of the valley. TRADER ANCHOR: the post is not in this file - TraderManager raises the quartermaster's kiosk (waystation_counter), the contracts board and the quartermaster from the region's `trader:waystation_9` spawn feature. Put that spawn at plan (18.0, 21.04) with the placement's facing: spawn pos = origin + Vector2(18.0, 21.04).rotated(deg_to_rad(rotation)), spawn yaw = -rotation (TraderDef.spawn_in(), in_poi). The kiosk then stands in the hatch recess (plan cells 16-19 x 16-18, its origin at (18.0, 17.04), backed onto the quartermaster's store), the quartermaster inside it at (17.7, 16.99), and the contracts board in the forecourt at (24.0, 22.54); keep those clear. The def's ring of hesco, towers and floodlights is not raised inside this building (TraderManager.in_building). Route: forecourt -> notice board -> guard room -> the hall on the wall line -> the Program stores (loot room) -> the radio room -> up the stair -> the lookout deck and its floodlight.",
