   "author": "Hollowmere team",
   "story": "Waystation 9 was a relay post on the Cordon line before it was anything else: a block of a building cast into the wall where the river runs out of the valley under it, a radio room on the outside, a hall along the line itself, a deck on top with a floodlight that sweeps the valley side every night. When the Remand Program came it set its quartermaster up in the recess by the guard-room door with a hatch, a price board and a list of contracts, and the post became the only place in the valley that still pays. The guards sleep in shifts in the bunk rooms, keep the floods on a generator and the radio on a battery bank, fly the lifts out from the strip on the far side, and never open the gate. Salvagers trade at the hatch. Nobody from the valley side has been through the building to the other side, and the standing orders on the guard-room desk say nobody will.",
